{"version":"0.12.12","prev_tag":"v0.12.11","target":"default","tag_prefix":"","area_scope":[],"commits":[{"sha":"52738bf010f0a30ee8d371740142ee2db827c10e","title":"Remove skill capability frontmatter from Task lifecycle validation — Make Task lifecycle validity structural (#1212)","files":["docs/authoring.md","docs/lf.md","docs/waves.md","rust/loopflow/src/bin/lf.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/implement.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/ship-5whys.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/execution.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/flow.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/launch.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/prompt.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/install.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/discovery.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/ask_comments.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/land.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pr.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/migrations.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/migrations/drafts/remove_task_lifecycle_outcome__f6a698c6969573c74a7c3016dec3bc88.sql","rust/loopflow/src/store/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite/children.rs","rust/loopflow/src/task/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/task/runner.rs","rust/loopflow/src/task/runner/shipping_lifecycle_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/flow_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/land_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/pr_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/support/mod.rs","scripts/materialize_rust_tests.py"]}],"merged_prs":[{"number":1212,"title":"Remove skill capability frontmatter from Task lifecycle validation — Make Task lifecycle validity structural","body":"Linear Task: [LOO-230](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-230/remove-skill-capability-frontmatter-from-task-lifecycle-validation)\n\n## Summary\n\n- make Task lifecycle validity structural instead of skill-declared\n- gate default feature work at design review and configured-path demo\n- preserve Linear Task identity across publish, refresh, land, and serial PRs\n\n## Proof\n\n- cargo test -p loopflow task_lifecycle --lib\n- cargo test -p loopflow --test pr_tests\n- cargo test -p loopflow --test land_tests\n- cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings\n- uv run python scripts/check_migrations.py","files":[],"additions":621,"deletions":314,"changed_files":29,"merge_commit":"52738bf010f0a30ee8d371740142ee2db827c10e"}],"decisions":null,"previous_release_notes":"# v0.12.11\n\n<!-- loopflow:release-notes=narrative;gate=safe -->\n\nv0.12.11 makes local Ask review feel native in Ghostty without changing the session model underneath. On macOS, `lf ask open` now gathers Asks into one dedicated Ghostty window, reuses named tabs, and focuses the requested session instead of presenting a tmux-linked Ask hub. Other terminals and remote presentation paths keep their existing behavior.\n\n## Review local Asks in one Ghostty window\n\nGhostty now owns the presentation layer while tmux continues to preserve each Ask as a distinct session. Reopening or concurrently presenting Asks therefore converges on the existing window and tabs rather than creating duplicate review surfaces.\n\n- Set `LF_EXTERNAL_TERMINAL=Ghostty` and run `lf ask open ask_...` to open or reattach an Ask in its named tab.\n- Loopflow remembers a dedicated Ghostty Ask window and focuses the requested tab when it already exists.\n- Concurrent presentations are serialized so they do not create duplicate windows or tabs.\n- Reattaching an existing Ask removes launcher scripts that are no longer needed.\n- Each Ask retains its own tmux session; only its local macOS presentation changes.\n\n## Operational notes\n\n- Native Ghostty tab control depends on macOS Automation permission. If access is denied, `lf ask open` reports guidance for enabling it.\n- The new routing applies only when Ghostty is selected as the external terminal. Other terminal integrations and remote Ask presentation are unchanged.","source_limits":{"context_bytes":131072,"commits":256,"merged_prs":200,"files_per_change":100,"area_scopes":32,"name_bytes":256,"title_bytes":300,"path_bytes":512,"pr_body_bytes":4096,"decisions_bytes":16384,"previous_release_notes_bytes":16384,"release_notes_bytes":61440},"omissions":{"commits":0,"merged_prs":0,"commit_files":0,"pr_files":0,"area_scopes":0,"text_bytes":0,"decisions_bytes":0,"previous_release_notes_bytes":0}}